ut0":{"type":"float","value":20}},"hidden":[],"name":"Float"},"71":{"attributes":{"font-size":{"type":"number","value":19},"text":{"type":"text","value":"FILTERING MIDI\n\nMIDI data contains all kinds of data like the channel, the controller, control change values (known as CC values), pitch, velocity and many more. Most of the time you don't need half of that data. So we implemented a lot of nodes that filter the data for you.\n\nThe small nodes like Pitch and Channel extract a single value from midi data, but they exctract this data from all channels. So if you have multiple channels of midi data comming in you might want to filter it with either the Midi Read nodes or Midi filter nodes.\n\nThe Midi filter nodes are for all you midi-pro's out there that know exactly what they want. You can filter the pitch and channel you want to recieve. This means there will be only one key on one channel that is being used. This is the way to go if you are building a custom midi controller in Wire.\n\nConnect a Midi controller to use the example."}},"bounds":{"height":257,"width":1046.9403076171875,"x":-160.19061279296875,"y":-397.842864990234375},"class":{"id":"77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374","version":0},"clock":"video","constants":{},"hidden":[],"name":"Comment"},"73":{"attributes":{"instances":{"type":"number","value":1}},"bounds":{"height":82,"width":130,"x":-83.18505859375,"y":103.7564239501953125},"class":{"id":"77697265-5275-4BB0-97B0-DBEEFD85997B","version":0},"clock":"video","constants":{"input":{"type":"midi","value":null}},"hidden":["input"],"name":"MIDI In"},"74":{"attributes":{"instances":{"type":"number","value":1},"normalize":{"type":"bool","value":true}},"bounds":{"height":82,"width":195,"x":224.6279296875,"y":696.60498046875},"class":{"id":"77697265-2F2C-47A5-8DA4-065DAE816AB2","version":0},"clock":"video","constants":{"channel":{"type":"integer","value":0},"controller":{"type":"integer","value":20},"input":{"type":"midi","value":null}},"hidden":[],"name